{"name":"Sierra Madre","hex":"#c2bcae","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sierra Madre","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Los Angeles County, California, United States.","A number of mountain ranges:\nin southwestern California: Sierra Madre (California)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sierra_Madre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sierra Madre Occidental","blocks":[{"text":"The Sierra Madre Occidental is a major mountain range system which runs northwest–southeast through northwestern and western Mexico, and along the Gulf of California. The Sierra Madre is part of the American Cordillera, an almost continuous chain of mountain ranges that forms the western \"backbone\" of the Americas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Sierra_Madre_Occidental.jpg/330px-Sierra_Madre_Occidental.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Madre_Occidental"},{"title":"Sierra Madre Oriental","blocks":[{"text":"The Sierra Madre Oriental is a mountain range located in northeastern Mexico. The Sierra Madre Oriental is part of the American Cordillera, a chain of mountain ranges (cordillera) that consists of an almost continuous sequence of mountain ranges that form the western \"backbone\" of North America, Central America, South America, and Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Cerros_Sierra_Madre_Oriental.jpg/330px-Cerros_Sierra_Madre_Oriental.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Madre_Oriental"},{"title":"Sierra Madre (Philippines)","blocks":[{"text":"The Sierra Madre is the longest mountain range in the Philippines. Spanning over 540 kilometers (340 mi), it runs from the province of Cagayan down to the province of Quezon in a north-south direction on the eastern portion of Luzon, the largest island of the archipelago. It is bordered by the Pacific Ocean to the east, Cagayan Valley to the northwest, Central Luzon to the midwest, and Calabarzon to the southwest. Some communities east of the mountain range, along the coast, are less developed and so remote that they can only be accessed by taking a plane or a boat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/View_south_of_the_northern_Sierra_Madre_from_peak_of_Mt._Cagua_-_ZooKeys-266-001-g007.jpg/330px-View_south_of_the_northern_Sierra_Madre_from_peak_of_Mt._Cagua_-_ZooKeys-266-001-g007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Madre_(Philippines)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/A_Nyugati-Sierra_Madre_elhelyezked%C3%A9se.jpg/500px-A_Nyugati-Sierra_Madre_elhelyezked%C3%A9se.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/A_Nyugati-Sierra_Madre_elhelyezked%C3%A9se.jpg/500px-A_Nyugati-Sierra_Madre_elhelyezked%C3%A9se.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Nyugati-Sierra_Madre_elhelyezked%C3%A9se.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg/500px-Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg/1280px-Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg/500px-Barranca_del_cobre_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Copper Canyon in Chihuahua, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarranca_del_cobre_2.jpg"},{"srcset